==Trivia==
*Boraphim's name is a portmanteau of ''[[Bore]]'' and ''Seraphim'', the highest class of angel in Christianity.
*His Japanese name, Inoenjeru (イノエンジェル), is a portmanteau of 猪 ''inoshishi'' (wild boar) and エンジェル ''enjeru'' (angel).
*Prior to [[Version 15.0 Update|Version 15.0]], his description misspelled "record" as "recor'''t'''".
*He is most probably based on Japanese composer [[wikipedia:ja:キダ・タロー|Tarō Kida]]. Not only are they both famous composers with grey hair, but Boraphim's Japanese description says he's chief adviser of a certain famous detective agency, the same title held by Tarō Kida on ''[[wikipedia:Knight Scoop|Knight Scoop]]''.
**Additionally, the songs mentioned in his Japanese description are "Operation Nyamputer" and "Cat Dōraku", referencing how Tarō Kida famously composed music for the television series ''[[wikipedia:Operation Love|Operation Love]]'' and the restaurant [[wikipedia:Kani Dōraku|Kani Dōraku]].

